 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "notice",
   "text": "Draft for Jared's approval. Collected word for word from the city-wide rules paragraphs of the neighbourhood guides listed at the bottom (D-202); nothing new was added. Each guide keeps what is specific to it and links here.",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Buying anywhere in the Township of Langley? These are the rules that apply city-wide, by topic: property taxes, transfer tax and GST, floodplain, farmland and environmental rules, strata, co-op and age rules and zoning, suites and small-scale housing. The neighbourhood guides cover what is specific to each area. Rules change, so check anything that matters for your purchase with the Township of Langley and your lawyer before you remove subjects.",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Property taxes, transfer tax and GST in Township of Langley",
   "id": "taxes",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Property taxes — Township of Langley: property taxes and utility fees were due Thursday, July 2, 2026; a 5% penalty applies to current-year taxes unpaid at midnight July 2, 2026, with a further 5% at midnight September 3, 2026. The tax notice includes general Township taxes plus levies for roads, drainage, solid waste and capital projects and taxes collected for other authorities; utility fees are now billed separately."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "taxes"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Co-op occupancy rules are the co-op's own: listings state buyer acceptance by the co-op and a share purchase as conditions of buying into Pioneer Park; the provincial strata exemptions (spouse/partner, caregiver, legacy, defined children — SPA Regulation 7.01, expanded May 1, 2023) govern strata 55+ bylaws and do not automatically apply inside a co-operative."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "taxes"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Floodplain, farmland and environmental rules in Township of Langley",
   "id": "flood",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Subdivision + servicing requirements (Township): A subdivision angle on a village or edge lot must be scoped with the Township (Approving Officer process, heritage/design overlays and flood/ALR status first) before any value is placed on it."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Flood / pump-station diligence: Flood status drives insurance and lending on these parcels."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Strata, co-op and age rules in Township of Langley",
   "id": "strata",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Zoning, SSMUH and suites (Township): Zoning Bylaw No. 2500 governs. SSMUH Bylaw No. 6020 (adopted November 18, 2024) allows 3 units on eligible lots of 280 m² or smaller and 4 units on larger eligible lots up to 4,050 m²; lots over 4,050 m² are ineligible, and no 6-unit tier applies in the Township — duplexes are the baseline SSMUH form. A secondary suite in the Township is capped at 120 m² — the Township's own cap, never borrowed. A coach house is a fee-simple second unit under s.102, never strata. Servicing Bylaw 2019 No. 5382 is confirmed. SSMUH does not apply to pad tenancies and creates no added-unit right inside a co-op park."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "strata"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Coach houses are fee-simple s. 102 units, not strata: under Zoning Bylaw No. 2500, s. 102, a coach house is a second dwelling unit on a fee-simple lot, part of the same title as the principal house, and cannot be sold separately. Confirm the current s. 102 text with the Township before relying on a coach-house angle for a specific lot."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "strata"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "CRF minimum 10% (strata stock): Since November 1, 2023, a strata's annual budget must contribute at least 10% of the operating fund to the contingency reserve fund."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "strata"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "A coach house is a fee-simple second unit under Zoning Bylaw 2500 s.102 (the definition source) — never strata."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "strata"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Zoning, suites and small-scale housing in Township of Langley",
   "id": "zoning",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Zoning / OCP: R-CL s.403 = 220 m² minimum lot area to 464.5 m² maximum lot area (an urban-zone reference from Township of Langley Zoning Bylaw 2500; no R-CL ground is identified in this rural district)."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Suites and coach houses (Township): The \"15% of lot to max 100 m²\" coach/garden-suite rule is Abbotsford's, not the Township's, and is not applied here."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Zoning: Township of Langley Zoning Bylaw No. 2500: governs, with the s.110.1 minimums in. Get the parcel's zone from the Township/GeoSource first."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Zoning + plans: rural land is under Township of Langley Zoning Bylaw No. 2500. The Township Official Community Plan and the Rural Plan govern the district."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Confirm subdivision servicing (roads, water, sewer/septic, drainage) with the Township for the specific application."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "SSMUH — stated so it is not misapplied here"
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Other things to know about buying in Township of Langley",
   "id": "other",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Plans (Township standing frame): the Willoughby Community Plan originates as Bylaw 1836 (1979), now Schedule 6 to Bylaw 6200 (adopted Dec 1, 2025); Willoughby Plan Update Bylaws 6201/6202/6203 had first/second reading May 25, 2026 only, with a Public Hearing directed for June 15, 2026."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "other"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Foreclosure / court-ordered sale: settled court process — Supreme Court Civil Rules 21-7 / 13-5, Practice Direction PD-66, Form 60."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "other"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Federal non-Canadian purchase prohibition — vacant land: Get advice on the current official text for the specific parcel."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "other"
  },
